IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `ei4-part-vi-proceedings-and-evidence`

-- Tests of ei4-part-vi-proceedings-and-evidence.l4 (Act ss 129 to 134). Expected values are written by hand from the text of the
-- section; none is copied from the module's output.

§ `s 129 -- privilege`

-- 129: written, oral or documentary evidence required for the proper determination of entitlement, given to the Commission.
#ASSERT `s 129 the giving of the evidence is an occasion of qualified privilege` TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- 129: evidence not required for that determination is outside the section.
#ASSERT NOT `s 129 the giving of the evidence is an occasion of qualified privilege` TRUE TRUE FALSE
-- 129: something said to someone other than the Commission.
#ASSERT NOT `s 129 the giving of the evidence is an occasion of qualified privilege` FALSE TRUE TRUE
-- 129: not evidence of any of the three kinds.
#ASSERT NOT `s 129 the giving of the evidence is an occasion of qualified privilege` TRUE FALSE TRUE

§ `s 130 -- default`

-- 130: someone's failure or neglect costs another person the right to claim benefits: the Commission may nevertheless pay.
#ASSERT `s 130 the Commission may nevertheless pay the benefits` TRUE TRUE
-- 130: no failure or neglect by anyone.
#ASSERT NOT `s 130 the Commission may nevertheless pay the benefits` FALSE TRUE
-- 130: a failure, but nobody lost the right because of it.
#ASSERT NOT `s 130 the Commission may nevertheless pay the benefits` TRUE FALSE

§ `s 131 -- question under section 90`

-- 131(1)(a): a question specified in section 90 arises and the authorized officer has not decided it: the court must refer it and defer.
#ASSERT `s 131(1)(a) the court must refer the question to an authorized officer of the Canada Revenue Agency and defer further proceedings until the ruling is received` TRUE FALSE
-- 131(1)(a): already decided by the officer: no referral is needed.
#ASSERT NOT `s 131(1)(a) the court must refer the question to an authorized officer of the Canada Revenue Agency and defer further proceedings until the ruling is received` TRUE TRUE
-- 131(1)(a): no such question.
#ASSERT NOT `s 131(1)(a) the court must refer the question to an authorized officer of the Canada Revenue Agency and defer further proceedings until the ruling is received` FALSE FALSE
-- 131(1)(b): on receipt of the ruling, proceed.
#ASSERT `s 131(1)(b) the court must proceed with the hearing and judgment` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 131(1)(b) the court must proceed with the hearing and judgment` TRUE FALSE
-- 131(2)(a): an appeal under section 91 is made: defer judgment until the decision of the Minister of National Revenue is received.
#ASSERT `s 131(2)(a) the court must defer judgment until the decision of the Minister of National Revenue is received` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 131(2)(a) the court must defer judgment until the decision of the Minister of National Revenue is received` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 131(2)(a) the court must defer judgment until the decision of the Minister of National Revenue is received` FALSE FALSE
-- 131(2)(b): an appeal under section 103: defer judgment until the decision of the Tax Court of Canada is received.
#ASSERT `s 131(2)(b) the court must defer judgment until the decision of the Tax Court of Canada is received` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 131(2)(b) the court must defer judgment until the decision of the Tax Court of Canada is received` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 131(2)(b) the court must defer judgment until the decision of the Tax Court of Canada is received` FALSE FALSE

§ `s 132 -- question for the Commission`

-- 132(1): a question the Commission could decide arises: refer it and defer until the Commission decides.
#ASSERT `s 132(1) the court must refer the question to the Commission and defer further proceedings until the Commission's decision is received` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 132(1) the court must refer the question to the Commission and defer further proceedings until the Commission's decision is received` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 132(1) the court must refer the question to the Commission and defer further proceedings until the Commission's decision is received` FALSE FALSE
-- 132(2): an appeal from the Commission's decision is pending: defer until the appeal decision is received.
#ASSERT `s 132(2) the court must defer further proceedings until the appeal decision is received` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 132(2) the court must defer further proceedings until the appeal decision is received` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 132(2) the court must defer further proceedings until the appeal decision is received` FALSE FALSE
-- 132(3): on receipt of the decision, proceed.
#ASSERT `s 132(3) the court must proceed with the hearing and judgment` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 132(3) the court must proceed with the hearing and judgment` FALSE
-- 132(3): in proceedings under the Act the decision is conclusive, except in accordance with the Federal Courts Act.
#ASSERT `s 132(3) the decision is conclusive` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 132(3) the decision is conclusive` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 132(3) the decision is conclusive` FALSE FALSE

§ `s 133 -- repealed`

#EVAL `s 133 repealed, and therefore not encoded`

§ `s 134 -- evidence of documents`

-- 134(1)(a): a resolution or record of the Commission, certified by a Commissioner or the Secretary.
#ASSERT `s 134(1)(a) the document is a resolution, record or proceeding certified by a Commissioner or the Secretary of the Commission` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 134(1)(a) the document is a resolution, record or proceeding certified by a Commissioner or the Secretary of the Commission` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 134(1)(a) the document is a resolution, record or proceeding certified by a Commissioner or the Secretary of the Commission` FALSE TRUE
-- 134(1)(b): a document in the Commission's custody (i), or an entry in its books (ii), certified by the Commission or an employee.
#ASSERT `s 134(1)(b) the document is a document or entry certified by the Commission or a person employed in the administration of this Act` TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `s 134(1)(b) the document is a document or entry certified by the Commission or a person employed in the administration of this Act` FALSE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 134(1)(b) the document is a document or entry certified by the Commission or a person employed in the administration of this Act` TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 134(1)(b) the document is a document or entry certified by the Commission or a person employed in the administration of this Act` FALSE FALSE TRUE
-- 134(1)(c): a certified statement of the amount of contributions or benefits.
#ASSERT `s 134(1)(c) the document is a certified statement of an amount paid, payable or owing` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 134(1)(c) the document is a certified statement of an amount paid, payable or owing` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 134(1)(c) the document is a certified statement of an amount paid, payable or owing` FALSE TRUE
-- 134(1)(d): a copy of an employer's records certified by an inspector to whom they were produced.
#ASSERT `s 134(1)(d) the document is a copy or extract of an employer's records certified by an inspector or other person employed in the administration of this Act` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 134(1)(d) the document is a copy or extract of an employer's records certified by an inspector or other person employed in the administration of this Act` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 134(1)(d) the document is a copy or extract of an employer's records certified by an inspector or other person employed in the administration of this Act` FALSE TRUE
-- 134(1): any one of (a) to (d), in proceedings under the Act, is evidence of the facts appearing in the document.
#ASSERT `s 134(1) the document is evidence of the facts appearing in it without proof of the signature or official character of the person appearing to have signed the certificate and without further proof` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 134(1) the document is evidence of the facts appearing in it without proof of the signature or official character of the person appearing to have signed the certificate and without further proof` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 134(1) the document is evidence of the facts appearing in it without proof of the signature or official character of the person appearing to have signed the certificate and without further proof` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 134(1) the document is evidence of the facts appearing in it without proof of the signature or official character of the person appearing to have signed the certificate and without further proof` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE
-- 134(1): a document within none of the four paragraphs, or proceedings not under the Act.
#ASSERT NOT `s 134(1) the document is evidence of the facts appearing in it without proof of the signature or official character of the person appearing to have signed the certificate and without further proof` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 134(1) the document is evidence of the facts appearing in it without proof of the signature or official character of the person appearing to have signed the certificate and without further proof` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- 134(2): a certificate that a notice was sent by mail is evidence that the addressee received it in the ordinary course of the mails.
#ASSERT `s 134(2) the certificate is evidence that the notice, request, demand or other document was received by the addressee in the ordinary course of the mails` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 134(2) the certificate is evidence that the notice, request, demand or other document was received by the addressee in the ordinary course of the mails` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 134(2) the certificate is evidence that the notice, request, demand or other document was received by the addressee in the ordinary course of the mails` FALSE TRUE
-- 134(3): a certified print from a film or electronic record the Commission made for a permanent record.
#ASSERT `s 134(3) the print is admissible in evidence for all purposes for which the recorded document would be admitted` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 134(3) the print is admissible in evidence for all purposes for which the recorded document would be admitted` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 134(3) the print is admissible in evidence for all purposes for which the recorded document would be admitted` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 134(3) the print is admissible in evidence for all purposes for which the recorded document would be admitted` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 134(3) the print is admissible in evidence for all purposes for which the recorded document would be admitted` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- 134(4): a document in electronic form is a document for the purposes of section 134, as is one in any other form.
#ASSERT `s 134(4) the thing is a document for the purposes of section 134` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 134(4) the thing is a document for the purposes of section 134` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 134(4) the thing is a document for the purposes of section 134` FALSE FALSE
